{"event": "agent_result", "task": "single-agent", "role": "single_agent", "result": {"report": {"incident_id": "github-token-036", "outcome": "probable_cause", "hypotheses": [{"description": "Most likely cause: the new GitHub relay incorrectly requires a raw provider access token from the connected-account response, but GitHub connected-account responses redact that token by design. The connection remains active and authenticated tool execution still works, so the relay misclassifies a healthy connection as unauthenticated.", "supporting_evidence": ["ev_349e9e66af16", "ev_1947c9b8c84d", "ev_c5af76d59927", "ev_09a96d0607b0"], "contradicting_evidence": [], "confidence": "high", "assumptions": ["The blocked cedar business operations correspond to the relay path described in the complaint, not a separate unobserved failure mode.", "The sandbox controlled comparison is representative of the production relay configuration difference."]}, {"description": "Alternative considered: a GitHub/provider outage or invalid connection/authentication state. This is less likely because the observed connection is active, authenticated tool execution succeeds, and a comparison tenant shows the same provider available with unrelated reads succeeding.", "supporting_evidence": ["ev_1947c9b8c84d"], "contradicting_evidence": ["ev_349e9e66af16", "ev_c5af76d59927"], "confidence": "high", "assumptions": ["The successful tool execution and read path are sufficient indicators that provider auth was usable at the time of observation."]}, {"description": "Alternative considered: an internal regression from a contemporaneous deployment. Evidence is weak because the only observed deployment is an unrelated support-dashboard release, not tool-executor.", "supporting_evidence": ["ev_36037a947c61", "ev_24d1a211a924"], "contradicting_evidence": ["ev_1947c9b8c84d"], "confidence": "low", "assumptions": ["No unobserved tool-executor deployment occurred within the incident window."]}], "recommended_actions": ["redacted_token_relay_design_remediation", "collect_missing_telemetry", "monitor_provider"], "limitations": ["Observed logs are sparse for the exact failed relay job; the canonical record shows the mechanism state but not a provider-side call attempt.", "The empty connections query is not treated as proof of absence because derived connection views are not independent corroboration.", "Historical similarity to an earlier provider outage is analogy only and not current proof."]}, "ranked_cause_codes": ["redacted_token_relay_design", "provider_failure", "unconfirmed_change"], "findings": [{"code": "mechanism_observation", "statement": "At the incident time for tenant cedar, the GitHub connected account was active and tool execution succeeded, but the relay required a raw token while the connected-account token field was REDACTED. This directly matches a design mismatch rather than a broken connection.", "citations": [{"evidence_id": "ev_672196ccc3ae", "record_id": "github-token-036:logs:0"}]}, {"code": "controlled_comparison", "statement": "In the controlled sandbox comparison, the original condition failed with the same pattern (active connection, REDACTED token, relay_requires_raw_token=true), while the corrected condition succeeded when the relay no longer required the raw token and instead used the authenticated proxy path.", "citations": [{"evidence_id": "ev_c5af76d59927", "record_id": "github-token-036:reproduce:0"}, {"evidence_id": "ev_c5af76d59927", "record_id": "github-token-036:reproduce:1"}]}, {"code": "verification_control", "statement": "Public product knowledge states that GitHub connected-account responses redact provider tokens while authenticated execution remains available, which explains why Composio tool executions work even though the relay cannot extract a raw token.", "citations": [{"evidence_id": "ev_349e9e66af16", "record_id": "github-token-036:knowledge:0"}]}, {"code": "tenant_impact", "statement": "Impact appears tenant-specific in the observed window: cedar shows 365 business operations blocked, queue depth 99, and p95 latency 1320 ms despite 0 request failures, while comparison tenant maple shows 0 blocked operations, queue depth 0, and p95 latency 160 ms.", "citations": [{"evidence_id": "ev_9cd316fe337a", "record_id": "github-token-036:metrics:0"}, {"evidence_id": "ev_710404032c95", "record_id": "github-token-036:metrics:1"}]}, {"code": "provider_isolation", "statement": "A provider-wide GitHub outage is not supported by the observed records: a comparison tenant had the same provider available with unrelated reads succeeding, and cedar's own authenticated tool execution also returned 200.", "citations": [{"evidence_id": "ev_1947c9b8c84d", "record_id": "github-token-036:logs:0"}, {"evidence_id": "ev_1947c9b8c84d", "record_id": "github-token-036:logs:1"}]}], "action_codes": ["redacted_token_relay_design_remediation", "collect_missing_telemetry", "monitor_provider"]}}
